<h1 id="website-admin-guide">Website Admin Guide</h1>
<h2 id="welcome">Welcome!</h2>
<p>This guide will walk you through everything you can do on the West
Baton Rouge Presbyterian Church website. You do not need any special
computer skills to use it. If you can send an email, you can do
everything in this guide.</p>
<p>A few things to keep in mind before you start:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>You can't break anything permanently.</strong> Almost
everything can be edited or undone. If you make a mistake, you can
always go back and fix it.</li>
<li><strong>Nothing you do here affects your computer.</strong>
Everything happens on the website itself. Your photos, your documents,
your files — none of that is touched.</li>
<li><strong>When in doubt, save and look.</strong> After you save
something, you can always click over to see how it looks to the public,
and then come back to edit it again.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2 id="1-signing-in">1. Signing In</h2>
<p>Before you can make any changes to the website, you need to sign in.
Think of this like unlocking the door to the office — the public can
look through the window, but only you have the key.</p>
<p><strong>To sign in:</strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>Open your web browser (the program you use to look at websites — it
might be Chrome, Edge, Firefox, or Safari).</li>
<li>Go to the church website address.</li>
<li>Look for the <strong>Staff Sign In</strong> link, in the bottom
footer area.</li>
<li>Type in your <strong>email address</strong> and your
<strong>password</strong>.</li>
<li>Click the <strong>Sign in</strong> button.</li>
</ol>
<p>Once you are signed in, you will notice a new item appear in
the navigation bar at the top of the page: <strong>Dashboard</strong>. This is a link to your admin-only tools.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> If you close the browser and come back later,
you may need to sign in again. That is normal and keeps the site
secure.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
